# The runtime closure a user installs (plan D5, hash-pinned install
# path; the offline bundle of plan P4-D409 is built from its lock). This
# file holds ONLY what synthtwin needs to run: the development and build
# tooling lives in requirements-dev.in.
#
# The floors here must match the ones declared in pyproject.toml, and the
# ROOTS here must match them too: a package this file names is a package
# an institutional install puts on somebody's machine, whatever another
# library happens to depend on. The four roots and the zone each may run
# in are argued in pyproject.toml's comment (plans P1-D2, P2-D8, P4-D409,
# P4-D410). tests/test_dependencies.py fails if either drifts.
--only-binary :all:
